WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.400 --> 00:00:07.380
Bacteria have no meiosis and make no zygote.

2
00:00:08.000 --> 00:00:14.560
Yet in 1946, two E. coli strains were mixed, and each strain could not make several

3
00:00:14.560 --> 00:00:19.140
nutrients. A few cells grew on a plate that supplied none of them.

4
00:00:20.060 --> 00:00:22.500
Neither strain alone gave a single colony.

5
00:00:23.260 --> 00:00:25.040
So where did the genes come from?

6
00:00:25.700 --> 00:00:28.880
How does DNA get from one bacterium into another?

7
00:00:29.750 --> 00:00:31.890
One route is conjugation.

8
00:00:32.390 --> 00:00:36.890
A donor cell touches a recipient and passes DNA straight across.

9
00:00:37.790 --> 00:00:42.190
In E. coli, the donor carries F, a small circle of DNA.

10
00:00:43.190 --> 00:00:45.330
Now and then, F joins the chromosome.

11
00:00:46.150 --> 00:00:48.090
That cell is called Hfr.

12
00:00:49.350 --> 00:00:54.210
Transfer starts inside F, and pulls the chromosome after it in a fixed order.

13
00:00:55.033 --> 00:00:58.693
Wollman and Jacob turned that order into a map.

14
00:00:59.533 --> 00:01:02.693
They mixed Hfr donors with F− recipients.

15
00:01:03.653 --> 00:01:06.853
At set times, they broke the pairs apart in a blender.

16
00:01:07.753 --> 00:01:11.933
Then they plated the recipients on medium where only recombinants grow.

17
00:01:12.893 --> 00:01:17.653
Each donor gene appeared only in samples taken after a characteristic time.

18
00:01:18.416 --> 00:01:20.636
Take one Hfr strain.

19
00:01:21.676 --> 00:01:24.056
Marker a first appears at 8 minutes.

20
00:01:25.016 --> 00:01:31.256
Marker b appears at 14, marker c at 20, and marker d at 31.

21
00:01:32.376 --> 00:01:36.736
If transfer runs at a steady rate, the time of entry is a position.

22
00:01:37.436 --> 00:01:40.896
So the gaps are 6, 6, and 11 minutes.

23
00:01:41.816 --> 00:01:50.716
A second Hfr strain gives d at 4 minutes, c at 15, b at 21, and a at 27.

24
00:01:51.636 --> 00:01:54.256
The order runs backwards, and the times differ.

25
00:01:54.916 --> 00:01:57.956
But the gaps are 11, 6, and 6.

26
00:01:58.856 --> 00:02:00.996
Read in reverse, it is the same map.

27
00:02:01.876 --> 00:02:06.596
Its origin lies on the far side of d, so it transfers in the opposite orientation.

28
00:02:07.566 --> 00:02:13.726
Hfr strains with F at different sites, in either orientation, gave overlapping

29
00:02:13.726 --> 00:02:17.026
orders. Those orders closed into a circle.

30
00:02:18.206 --> 00:02:22.626
Jacob and Wollman estimated that the whole chromosome would take about 100 minutes

31
00:02:22.626 --> 00:02:24.306
to enter at a constant rate.

32
00:02:24.986 --> 00:02:29.126
That is why the E. coli map runs from 0 to 100 minutes.

33
00:02:30.006 --> 00:02:32.786
Keep this rule: the gaps are the map.
